-Owner skill: `skill://ipc-contract`. Thin Tauri shell over `yamt_session::MergeSession` and `yamt_lsp_host::Host`, or with `--diff` over `yamt_compare::TabStore` (plan §2 #93–#97, #101): `lib.rs` (`run`, `export_bindings`) shared by both bins; `graphics.rs` (NVIDIA guard: the first statement of `run()`, the project's one `unsafe` line, plan §2 #43), `args.rs` (`yamt [--repo <path>]` → `Merge`, `yamt --diff` → `Compare`; `--diff` with `--repo` is a usage error, `--help`/`--version` win), `appimage.rs` (inside an AppImage — `APPIMAGE` and `APPDIR` set and the binary under `$APPDIR` — a relative `--repo` is resolved against `OWD`; never chdir, WebKit's helper paths are relative to `$APPDIR/usr`; never called for `Compare`), `outcome.rs` (start-up decision, exit status 0/1/2; the close ending, `ending_when_git_is_done` — `ending_on_close` once `lock_when_git_is_done` lets go: `Finished(kind)` 0 with `<operation> finished`, `Aborted(kind)` 1 with `<operation> aborted` (`merge aborted` for a merge), reading and writing nothing; `Held` lists through `refresh_stop` and counts git's view, a `MovedOn` there counting the stop git moved on to like `MovedOn`; `MovedOn` opens the stop git is at only to count its unmerged files, settling nothing), `merge.rs` (`Merge` = `Held(Box<MergeSession>)` | `Running(kind)` | `MovedOn { root, highest_disk_version }` | `Aborted(kind)` | `Finished(kind)`, the app's merge state as `MergeState` = `Mutex<Merge>`; `session()` answers `GitRunning`, `StopMovedOn`, `MergeAborted` or `MergeFinished` outside `Held` — the one state → refusal mapping, also what a worker hand-over refuses with; `has_ended()` is true only for `Finished`/`Aborted`; `list_stop` opens the new stop after a move with `MergeSession::open_after(root, highest_disk_version)`, so its disk versions start above the old session's and a write meant for the old stop is refused (#1383), becomes `MovedOn` when git moved on, and builds `Listing::Files` from session's `StopList` by an exhaustive destructure, so a new field does not compile until it is listed; every `MovedOn` is built by `moved_on(&session)` (root and `highest_disk_version()`); `abort_operation`/`continue_operation` hand the session to a `spawn_blocking` worker while `Running` and put the outcome back: refused → `Held`, the stop moved on outside yamt (`StopMovedOn`) → `MovedOn`, so the next `list_stop` opens git's stop (#1440), stopped → `MovedOn`, a panicked worker → `MovedOn` built before the hand-over, answering `StopMovedOn` like every later call (the window goes to the next stop) and logging the join error with `tracing::error!`; `lock_when_git_is_done` makes the close ending wait for git; plan §2 #74, #88, #89; its tests in `merge/tests.rs`), `compare.rs` (the compare window, plan §2 #94/#95/#97: `manage_store_in` opens `TabStore` and manages it as `CompareState` in `<data_dir>/yamt/compare/` before any window, its failure the one line `yamt --diff` ends with (exit 2); `CompareState` = `Mutex<TabStore>`; the eight commands `open_compare`, `load_tab`, `set_column`, `add_tab`, `close_tab`, `rename_tab`, `set_tab_language`, `show_tab`; `load_tab`/`set_column` run on a `spawn_blocking` worker that locks the store only to call it, then builds the reply (`tab_texts`/`comparison`, the diff) after the lock is released; a worker that panicked answers `WorkerStopped`), `clipboard.rs` (`read_clipboard(selection: ClipboardSelection)` → the text or `None`, for both windows, no managed state, plan §2 #99: on Linux GTK's text request (`gtk::Clipboard::request_text`), started on the main thread by `run_on_main_thread` and waited for on a `spawn_blocking` worker, so a hung owner never blocks the window; it never asks GTK for the selection's format list — no `request_targets`, `wait_for_targets`, `wait_is_*_available`, `wait_for_contents`, `request_contents` — since WebKitGTK 2.54 crashes on a failed one; other systems answer `None`), `window.rs` (one window per run, merge or compare, built by one 